<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!DOCTYPE translationbundle>
<translationbundle lang="en-GB">
<translation id="1207194515919037363">The security module on this device is not working.

Please refer to this URL for more information:

https://www.google.com/chromeos/recovery</translation>
<translation id="1600199746926806589">Your device will automatically be enrolled into the domain shown below.
Please verify that it is correct.</translation>
<translation id="2701006671590617571">You are about to recover your computer. Please make sure that it is
plugged in to a power source.

If you want to cancel recovery, press the power button and hold it
down until the computer turns off (this takes up to 8 seconds).
It is safe to do this at any time during verification.</translation>
<translation id="2731700343119398978">Please wait…</translation>
<translation id="300775974721831513">The device owner requires this device to run with Chrome OS
verification turned on. You are trying to install an unofficial
Chrome OS recovery image, which does not pass verification.

For more information, refer to this URL:

https://www.google.com/chromeos/devmode</translation>
<translation id="3243756202241744259">Verifying the integrity of your recovery media…</translation>
<translation id="3283913352572436199">Your recovery media is configured for automatic setup after it reboots.

To proceed with automatic setup, press the Volume Up button. Otherwise,
press Volume Down. If you want to cancel recovery, press the power button
and hold it down until the device turns off (this takes up to 8 seconds).</translation>
<translation id="33938768013536853">Battery too low for update.

Please connect your Chromebook to a power socket. The update
will automatically begin as soon as the battery has enough charge.</translation>
<translation id="369510862371290019">Your recovery media is configured for automatic setup after it reboots.

To proceed with automatic setup, press the device's recovery switch.
If you want to cancel recovery, press the power button and hold it
down until the device turns off (this takes up to 8 seconds).</translation>
<translation id="3750930141330200643">You are using an out-of-date Chrome OS recovery image.

Please refer to this URL for instructions on how to create new
recovery media:

https://www.google.com/chromeos/recovery</translation>
<translation id="3946632524220974380">A developer key change is required to proceed; the process takes
5 minutes.</translation>
<translation id="436588829138218801">Chrome OS verification is turned off.

If this is unintentional, you should cancel recovery and disable
developer mode in order to enable verification. For more information,
refer to this URL:

https://www.google.com/chromeos/recovery</translation>
<translation id="4905949142713655149">An unexpected error has occurred. Please refer to this URL for
troubleshooting tips:

https://www.google.com/chromeos/recovery</translation>
<translation id="496201662522655493">System recovery is complete.

It is now safe to remove the recovery media. Your computer will
automatically restart shortly.</translation>
<translation id="537291066186627789">System recovery is complete.

Please remove the recovery media and your computer will restart
automatically.</translation>
<translation id="544118001572747892">Your computer does not appear to be a Chrome OS system!

This operation will delete any other operating system that you may have
installed and all the data; there will be no opportunity for backup.
If you have any data on this computer that you want to preserve, you
should cancel recovery.</translation>
<translation id="5512602676102820748">Battery too low for update.

Charging...

The update will automatically begin as soon as the battery has enough charge.</translation>
<translation id="6037207722716689331">Your recovery media is configured for automatic setup after it reboots.

To proceed with automatic setup, press Enter. Otherwise, press Escape.
If you want to cancel recovery, press the power button and hold it
down until the device turns off (this takes up to 8 seconds).</translation>
<translation id="6478314309353607985">The image on your recovery media is an unverified developer image.

Recovery will continue because verified boot is turned off.
If you later turn verification back on, you will need to repeat
recovery with an official Chrome OS image.</translation>
<translation id="816304391526917903">You are using an out-of-date official Chrome OS recovery image.

Recovery will continue because verification is turned off.
If you later turn verification back on, you will need to repeat
recovery with an up-to-date Chrome OS image.</translation>
<translation id="8596190965261846034">Installing update...

Please do not turn off the device.
It will automatically reboot when the update finishes.</translation>
<translation id="8728458033228603970">System recovery in progress…

This will take a few minutes. Please do not turn off the computer or
disconnect the power.</translation>
<translation id="8796495438384109098">System recovery is complete.

Please keep your recovery media plugged in until automatic setup is complete.
Your computer will automatically restart shortly to continue setup.</translation>
</translationbundle>